    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0558" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/124: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-23T18:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Referring to the second paragraph of your 98, June 17, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d505-f1"/> what is your estimate of the political situation as it
                    stands at present? Does the present regime give any indication of stability? Is
                        Dávila the real power in the
                    Government? What elements are supporting him, what is their strength and to what
                    extent do you think Dávila can rely on
                    them? What are the principal elements opposed to him? Are there any developments
                    regarding the possible return of Ibañez?
                    Your 104 June 20, 8 p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d505-f2"/> was protection
                    requested afforded?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
